globalThis.pzCourseExport="# KPV · course dossier\n\nRevision: Revision 81\ncourse:2904f98c-76ad-5d23-aa9a-bc89786561fd\ndocumented_course\nStart unknown · Off by 2024-10-21 · The October 21 account described a previous trial already stopped. Neither start nor last dose is dated. Final dose date unknown. Stopped by 2024-10-21. Exact final dose date unknown.\nDate-window anchor: No dated start or action\n\n## Baseline before the selected anchor\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Intended targets\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Actions and doses\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Course timing evidence\n\n- 2024-10-21 · stopped by · The October 21 account described a previous trial already stopped. Neither start nor last dose is dated.\n  Source · archive_messages:S1-M6\n- 2026-11-20 · stopped by · Confirmed off the regimen by this date. Exact last dose unknown.\n  Source · pz_regimen_snapshot:PZ-STACK-2026-11-20\n\n## Potential effects\n\n- Reported rapid improvement of constipation and gut pain during prior capsule trial; stopped after approximately two weeks. Later exposures occurred. · patient report\n  Source · archive_findings:S1-F6-5 | claim:80cf4e97-392c-5853-a0a2-79d54f012e79 | course · Source explicitly describes this particular trial or its follow-up. Read wording for attribution and competing exposures.\n\n## Potential effects reported outside a specific course\n\n- * KPV peptide, oral: more or less fixed constipation, went from 1-2x bowel movements per week to 1-2x per day · patient retrospective\n  Source · historical_entries:S3:treatment_response:196 | claim:5ad8da92-c46b-535b-8284-59ad040cd7d6 | entity · KPV; matching exposure wording, course or administration unestablished (representative record only)\n- Reported rapid improvement of constipation and gut pain during prior capsule trial; stopped after approximately two weeks. Later exposures occurred. · patient report\n  Source · archive_findings:S1-F6-5 | claim:8c4baa16-d84c-5dc4-be01-4aad68d8994f | entity · KPV; matching exposure wording, course or administration unestablished (representative record only)\n- The patient reported 1–2 bowel movements per day compared with one every other day previously, and described less fatty-appearing stool. · patient\n  Source · annotations:ANN-S1-10616 | claim:9c94809c-7059-5d7b-b80d-2255ebce8e76 | entity · KPV; matching exposure wording, course or administration unestablished (representative record only)\n- Reported or suspected association · The patient reported relief after KPV and charcoal in a multi-exposure episode. · unconfirmed\n  Source · diary_responses:S2-R-649 | claim:bc05bc25-1664-590f-8f9b-a68bc1c94923 | entity · Reviewed participant role in diary_responses:S2-R-649.\n- The patient recalled constipation since the start of long COVID and daily bowel movements during a period of improvement on KPV. They did not recall a corresponding improvement in their broader symptoms. · patient report\n  Source · archive_findings:S1-F2-55085 | claim:ca5de9dd-4857-52c6-9adb-a94f6324a1f7 | entity · KPV; matching exposure wording, course or administration unestablished (representative record only)\n\n## Source evidence and qualifications\n\n- [annotations:ANN-S1-10616] · reported 2024-12-31T07:09:36+01:00 · Bowel pattern during KPV · The patient reported 1–2 bowel movements per day compared with one every other day previously, and described less fatty-appearing stool. · patient · firsthand_subjective_report · This was an early response report. A later retrospective history gives a different earlier bowel frequency.\n- [annotations:ANN-S1-69941] · reported 2026-02-18T18:45:29+01:00 · Gut improvement without a higher baseline · The patient said that even when their gut improved greatly, their overall baseline did not change. · patient · firsthand_subjective_report · This observation qualifies any inference that relief of constipation or GI pain consistently improved the neurological illness.\n- [archive_findings:S1-F6-5] · reported 2024-10-21 · Reported rapid improvement of constipation and gut pain during prior capsule trial; stopped after approximately two weeks. Later exposures occurred.\n- [archive_messages:S1-M10352] · reported 2024-12-28T07:34:36+01:00 · btw i have started kpv last night. hope that has an effect soon · patient message · 2024-12-28T07:34:36+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M10616] · reported 2024-12-31T07:09:36+01:00 · one thing: i hope it's not just a fluke but the kpv has been working excellently so far. getting 1-2 bowel movements daily whereas it used to be every second day before. the stool is also more normal (was very fatty before) · patient message · 2024-12-31T07:09:36+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M6] · reported 2024-10-21T21:02:55+02:00 · actually i can answer those questions quite quickly as there isn't much. things that have helped: - nicergoline: old school vasodilator, noticeable improvement for the first 1.5 months, then effect slowly wore off. suggests neurological issues are at least partially circulation driven (see messages below) - MCT oil and possibly monolaurin: went from halfway bed bound to being more active - basic liposomal vitamins that i think raised my baseline energy - i'm taking a locally made probiotics and a liposomal pectin complex acting as a prebiotic, which have greatly improved my GI issues. went from dysbiosis and constant strong pain in both corners of the large intestines, slow motility and constipation to normal bowel movements and rare pains and rare constipation (so not fully healed yet). - KPV peptides did help with the constipation too but i went off them because was told they were not compatible with the above. - anti-histamine diet and in general lighter meals help: eating steak or anything more energy intensive to digest often triggered a brain burn. the energy requirement of digestion likely triggered dysautonomic symptoms -\u003e cerebral blood flow issue nothing has really helped my severe brainfog and brain burns, sadly. peptides: have tried a few more other than KPV but unfortunately i forgot which. they didn't help my neurological issues though. will check and let you know which ones. · patient message · 2024-10-21T21:02:55+02:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M69932] · reported 2026-02-18T18:42:33+01:00 · Researcher interpreted Enterosgel as unsuccessful in this case and prioritized D-lara and KPV, recalling a little benefit with KPV. The opening claim about gut treatment helping referred to a different person, as clarified subsequently. · researcher commentary · 2026-02-18T18:42:33+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M69941] · reported 2026-02-18T18:45:29+01:00 · I disagree actually Ever ever gut improved greatly my baseline remained unchanged · patient message · 2026-02-18T18:45:29+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M69945] · reported 2026-02-18T18:48:51+01:00 · Reported that targeting the gut had not improved their overall condition. · patient message · 2026-02-18T18:48:51+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M8151] · reported 2024-12-07T22:29:04+01:00 · The researcher discussed BPC-157 for suspected gut permeability, sometimes combined with VIP, and described peptides as adjuncts that should be selected for the particular case. They said mast-cell-associated inflammation could initially worsen with BPC. · researcher commentary · 2024-12-07T22:29:04+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M8160] · reported 2024-12-07T22:32:08+01:00 · that makes sense. i believe i tried Epithalon nose sprays – no effect, and KPV capsules, which immediately solved my constipation while i was on it for a few days. · patient message · 2024-12-07T22:32:08+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M9399] · reported 2024-12-18T02:28:14+01:00 · We need to improve gut slowly over a period of time. There is no quick fix for that unfortunately · researcher commentary · 2024-12-18T02:28:14+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M9403] · reported 2024-12-18T02:39:16+01:00 · kpv peptide worked *very* quickly when my gut was in pain every day. i'm really sad i stopped it after two weeks or so. have you had a chance to look into it! · patient message · 2024-12-18T02:39:16+01:00\n- [s1_quote_context:S1-M69941#1] · reported 2026-02-18T18:45:29+01:00 · unverified; see linked parent where identified\n- [s1_quote_context:S1-M8160#1] · reported 2024-12-07T22:32:08+01:00 · unverified; see linked parent where identified\n- [s1_quote_context:S1-M9403#1] · reported 2024-12-18T02:39:16+01:00 · unverified; see linked parent where identified";
